# Deferral

Deferral is an exception. Do not ship "temporary", "for now", "until v0.3", or "in a later Issue" unless a roadmap row with an ID names the work, the item is under **Intentionally out of scope** in `docs/roadmap.md`, or the design names the phase.

A row says when. A promise to file an Issue later does not.

Before saying that work stays in its row, find that row's ID in `docs/roadmap.md`. A sentence of the design that defers is held to the same: when the row a contract waits for does not exist, the work goes into a row before the sentence is written.

A recommendation to drop or defer work is not argued from what its result would be. "The measurement will not change the decision" is a result nobody has; the work exists to find it out. What may be put to the owner is what the work costs and what it is for.

A row that is `done` did everything its design section gives it. Before a row is closed, search `docs/design.ja.md` for its ID and title.

Not allowed:

- "Temporary until the next milestone" when that milestone's row does not name the split.
- Closing a milestone while a temporary gap is still in the code.
- A `TODO` comment that stands in for a roadmap row.

When a row becomes `done` or moves out of scope, search `docs/`, the READMEs, and `.cursor/rules/` for its title and keywords, and rewrite stale "until X" text in the same PR.
